  "lineage": "Pingju Northern Chinese regional opera tradition emerging in late-nineteenth-century Hebei province from the lianhualao folk-song-and-storytelling form. Distinguished from jingju by accessible vernacular Mandarin language, naturalistic realistic staging, and contemporary-life dramaturgical content (vs jingju's classical historical-and-mythological repertoire). The genre became a major popular-theatrical form in northern China through the early-twentieth-century commercial-theatre period. The post-1949 Beijing Pingju Theatre and Hebei Provincial Pingju Theatre consolidated the modern repertoire. Canonical play Yang Sanjie Gao Zhuang (The Story of Yang Sanjie) constitutes the type-specimen.",
